Fork
-----

fork() creates a new process by duplicating the calling process. The process is referred to as the child process. The calling process is referred to as the parent process.

pid_t fork(void);


#include <stdio.h>
#include <unistd.h>
int main() {

	printf("hi\n");
	fork();	// new process created
	printf("bye...\n");
}

